@Chaosus Everything you mentioned should now be fixed/implemented. 

Concerning the group input and output nodes: First I had a strict implementation which ensured exactly one input and one output node. However, that came with its own set of problems and was ugly in code. After that I came up with a general solution that allowed multiple(or none) input and output nodes, which simplified things a lot while providing an actual UX benefit. One could argue that multiple output nodes are not really that useful, but I think it has some value (and making an exception would reintroduce the problem I mentioned again). In Blender, you can have multiple output nodes, but only one is active at a time. This makes sense to me: You could build branches in your group, trying things out, and switching between output nodes - basically allowing you to have several versions of your group without any runtime cost, vaguely similar to conditional compilation.
Right now, just the first output node is selected and a warning is shown on the group instance node, so this feature needs to be implemented still. But I'd rather do this in a subsequent PR.

@KoBeWi Sorry, one of those was an oversight, but for the others I honestly can't remember. (Could be a missclick, since this GH thread is so slow in my browser, especially when all review comments are expanded; I'm literally writing my answers in notepad and copy them because the embedded text editors are unusable :) Does anyone else have this problem?)
Anyways, thanks for the thorough review! 

Rebased and once CI passes this should be ready to go.
